<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RUGBY UNION-SUPER 12 RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-SUPER 12 RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and standings</p>
<p>after round four of the Super 12 rugby union tournament.</p>
<p>Results:</p>
<p>ACT beat Canterbury 49-29</p>
<p>Free State beat Natal 45-40</p>
<p>Gauteng Lions beat New South Wales 36-27</p>
<p>Otago beat Northern Transvaal 27-7</p>
<p>Waikato beat Queensland 31-16</p>
<p>Table (tabulated under played, won, drawn, lost, points for,</p>
<p>points against, bonus points, total points :</p>
<p>    Gauteng Lions	 4   4   0   0   151   112    2    18</p>
<p>    Natal		   3   2   0   1   150   114    4    12</p>
<p>    Waikato		 4   3   0   1   103    86    0    12</p>
<p>    Auckland		3   2   1   0    90    71    1    11</p>
<p>    ACT		     4   2   0   2   135   127    3    11</p>
<p>    Free State	    4   2   0   2   115   112    1     9</p>
<p>    Northern Transvaal  4   1   1   2    93   134    2     8</p>
<p>    Wellington	    3   1   0   2    99    74    3     7</p>
<p>    Otago		   3   1   0   2    99   129    2     6</p>
<p>    New South Wales     3   1   0   2    78    77    1     5</p>
<p>    Canterbury	    3   1   0   2    56    91    1     5</p>
<p>    Queensland	    4   0   0   4    62   104    1     1</p>
<p>(Note: Gauteng Lions formerly Transvaal.</p>
</text>
